#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161789 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161997 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "84c1cf7c-e334-5173-8ae4-86af0dce56ab" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Median Given the CDF a Continuous Random Variable"}] :question/id #uuid "dd626772-dd96-5840-8375-9ace79fecf70" :question/math-academy-id "e-8237" :question/problem "Find the median of the random variable $X$ if the cumulative distribution function of $X$ is given by\n\n![](images/6c/6c54af85add7fd0b136f807ac3f65f84dabd948b21c16fcb4fb05fc41e3fab70.svg)" :question/worked-solution "The median of a random variable $X$ is the number $m$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X \\leq m) = \\dfrac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nP(X \\leq m) = F(m) = 1-\\dfrac{1}{m^4} , \\quad m \\geq 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the median is given by\n\n$$\n1-\\dfrac{1}{m^4} = \\dfrac{1}{2}\\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad m = \\sqrt[4]2.\n$$\n\nNote that we took the positive root because $m \\geq 1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161790 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161998 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a79c4207-c5d6-5386-818e-a7e532492732" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Median Given the PDF a Continuous Random Variable"}] :question/id #uuid "d22e7154-ac3c-5ac6-ad86-77a7eb08f82e" :question/math-academy-id "e-8238" :question/problem "Find the median of the random variable $X$ if the probability density function of $X$ is given by\n\n![](images/e3/e3eb6147bfde4d3e4c65bad5054fc311cf561c1c869530bbf693f362a057033d.svg)" :question/worked-solution "The median of a random variable $X$ is the number $m$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X \\leq m) = \\dfrac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le m) & ={\\int }_{1}^{m}\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}|}_{1}^{m} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{m}^{2}}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the median is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{{m}^{2}}+1 & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{m}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ m & =\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we took the positive root because $m \\geq 1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161791 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161999 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "563f7ff5-8ebb-5130-badb-f092fa348959" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quartile of a Continuous Random Variable"}] :question/id #uuid "3be25e37-7162-5565-86d2-47ea69c599ce" :question/math-academy-id "e-8239" :question/problem "Find, to three decimal places, the interquartile range of the random variable $X$ if the cumulative distribution function of $X$ is given by\n\n![](images/be/be9a31bab2f359a49dc4c334a1584cee4d60b0f353e65c45a92409f928102daf.svg)" :question/worked-solution "To find the interquartile range, we first need to find the lower quartile and the upper quartile.\n\nThe lower quartile of a random variable $X$ is the number $q_1$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X \\leq q_1) = \\dfrac{1}{4},\n$$\n\nand the upper quartile is the number $q_3$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X \\leq q_3) = \\dfrac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the lower quartile:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le {q}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ F({q}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ \\frac{1}{25}{q}_{1}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ {q}_{1}^{2} & =\\frac{25}{4} \\\\ {q}_{1} & =\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the upper quartile:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le {q}_{3}) & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ F({q}_{3}) & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ \\frac{1}{25}{q}_{3}^{2} & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ {q}_{3}^{2} & =\\frac{75}{4} \\\\ {q}_{3} & =\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the interquartile range is\n\n$$\nIQR = q_3 - q_1 =\\dfrac{5\\sqrt3}{2} - \\dfrac{5}{2}\\approx 1.830\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161792 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162000 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "84b181c4-fc23-5a68-8042-55f02b1e5e8a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Percentile of a Continuous Random Variable"}] :question/id #uuid "d4d4f78a-05e2-57cf-8630-110daa4b61da" :question/math-academy-id "e-8240" :question/problem "Find the $27$th percentile of the random variable $X$ if the probability distribution function of $X$ is given by\n![](images/4e/4ea6c51080e39f5ea4d293d0265c0b5ddf5001f638bd4177646f29e2140bf279.svg)" :question/worked-solution "The $100p$th percentile of a random variable $X$ is the number $x_p$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X \\leq x_p) = p.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we want to find the $27$th percentile, which corresponds to the decimal $p=0.27.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le {x}_{0.27}) & ={\\int }_{5}^{{x}_{0.27}}\\frac{2}{75}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{2}}{75}|}_{5}^{{x}_{0.27}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}_{0.27}^{2}}{75}-\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $27$th percentile is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}_{0.27}^{2}}{75}-\\frac{1}{3} & =0.27 \\\\ {x}_{0.27}^{2} & =75(\\frac{27}{100}+\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\ {x}_{0.27} & =6.727\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482516 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161997 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "84c1cf7c-e334-5173-8ae4-86af0dce56ab" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Median Given the CDF a Continuous Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1138d2b7-a3e3-5532-97b5-c5fc9d0129c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481818} {:answer/id #uuid "4b1dae7a-d1c2-5268-ab76-bb5800e65796" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt[3]{32}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481955} {:answer/id #uuid "62c8e9a7-f26a-5628-88e2-f271c7a23633" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{32}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482001} {:answer/id #uuid "a48a09bd-cecc-5482-94cb-5f60175e9e4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{32}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482164} {:answer/id #uuid "d675510a-f4a2-5e75-8380-eb715fc51139" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482286}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b1dae7a-d1c2-5268-ab76-bb5800e65796" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt[3]{32}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481955} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a8c632b-7961-5fad-8319-cad8210fb3f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482423}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "26759ee4-9182-5088-bdc1-26b84fc02211" :question/math-academy-id "q-125510" :question/problem "Find the median of the random variable $X$ if the cumulative distribution function of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0, \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{3}}{64}, & 0\\le x\\le 4, \\\\ 1, & x\\ge 4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The median of a random variable $X$ is the number $m$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X\\le m)=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nP(X\\le m)=F(m)=\\frac{{m}^{3}}{64},\\,0\\le m\\le 4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the median is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{m}^{3}}{64}=\\frac{1}{2}\\,⇒\\,m=\\sqrt[3]{32}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482551 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161997 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "84c1cf7c-e334-5173-8ae4-86af0dce56ab" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Median Given the CDF a Continuous Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bfcbbaa-a8cc-51e4-be1a-c7f73905315a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{34}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481797} {:answer/id #uuid "74401d18-1e97-5151-b206-bf19cb24f8a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt[4]{136}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482044} {:answer/id #uuid "9543e404-9adb-5088-a2f1-e2be2229a985" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt[3]{34}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482125} {:answer/id #uuid "e4851740-2d3d-54dc-b48c-3c099aec6c2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482317} {:answer/id #uuid "f028fb9b-aaf2-5ba7-81b1-86734cbf6171" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt[4]{34}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482346}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74401d18-1e97-5151-b206-bf19cb24f8a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt[4]{136}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482044} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa5b07f4-7bd6-5b7b-b298-c1c8eac0c1bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482467}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "72db930f-dc67-5772-9a58-607de1ef27a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-125515" :question/problem "Find the median of the random variable $X$ if the cumulative distribution function of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<2, \\\\ \\frac{1}{240}({x}^{4}-16), & 2\\le x\\le 4, \\\\ 1, & x>4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The median of a random variable $X$ is the number $m$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X\\le m)=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nP(X\\le m)=F(m)=\\frac{1}{240}({m}^{4}-16),\\,2\\le m\\le 4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the median is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{240}({m}^{4}-16)=\\frac{1}{2}\\,⇒\\,m=\\sqrt[4]{136}.\n$$\n\nNote that we took the positive root because $2\\le m\\le 4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482508 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161997 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "84c1cf7c-e334-5173-8ae4-86af0dce56ab" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Median Given the CDF a Continuous Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3050f898-36aa-5645-a5a4-af8b4ba8fde3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481894} {:answer/id #uuid "92a7b198-9238-51a4-b8ab-d4d1a87d50ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482120} {:answer/id #uuid "ca571706-b58d-5784-b937-566421c78a8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482255} {:answer/id #uuid "e38ccb96-44ea-55c6-99c9-dae1e3a87ad7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482315} {:answer/id #uuid "f88d6025-6a3c-5c70-abf4-3698342d3349" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482362}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3050f898-36aa-5645-a5a4-af8b4ba8fde3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481894} :answer-field/id #uuid "37430a3d-0d71-5551-a19e-aa1fdf2b1819" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482408}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "07427b74-a9a0-5dbd-ab84-a95a81a836e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-125516" :question/problem "Find the median of the random variable $X$ if the cumulative distribution function of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0, \\\\ \\frac{x}{3}, & 0\\le x\\le 2 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{4}}{195}+\\frac{38}{65}, & 2<x\\le 3, \\\\ 1, & x>3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The median of a random variable $X$ is the number $m$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X\\le m)=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nSince $F(2)=\\frac{2}{3}>\\frac{1}{2},$ we have $0\\le m\\le 2.$\n\nTherefore, the median is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{m}{3}=\\frac{1}{2}\\,⇒\\,m=\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482525 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162000 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "84b181c4-fc23-5a68-8042-55f02b1e5e8a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Percentile of a Continuous Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ab03d75-993a-5e56-a3b5-e9a96b0abe16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.49" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481793} {:answer/id #uuid "37007c7d-15c3-514b-a461-702523f7b376" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481912} {:answer/id #uuid "8b123b93-545f-51fb-8532-62a1a090adcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482099} {:answer/id #uuid "b4cd0f4f-3e7c-5169-b1c0-6d7b3ad093ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482201} {:answer/id #uuid "b8cf6423-b887-5ec3-83c1-58b408697ebe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482214}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4cd0f4f-3e7c-5169-b1c0-6d7b3ad093ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482201} :answer-field/id #uuid "21cbc6ee-ce3d-5b0e-a165-e71872b21032" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482396}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "36945eec-4c74-5f74-8f42-dd9a1f9a922a" :question/math-academy-id "q-125520" :question/problem "Find the $51.2$th percentile of the random variable $X$ if the probability distribution function of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{x},\\, & 0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The $100p$th percentile of a random variable $X$ is the number ${x}_{p}$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X\\le {x}_{p})=p.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we want to find the $51.2$th percentile, which corresponds to the decimal $p=0.512.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le {x}_{0.512}) & ={\\int }_{0}^{{x}_{0.512}}\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={{x}^{\\frac{3}{2}}|}_{0}^{{x}_{0.512}} \\\\  & ={x}_{0.512}^{\\frac{3}{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $51.2$th percentile is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{0.512}^{\\frac{3}{2}} & =0.512 \\\\ {x}_{0.512}^{\\frac{1}{2}} & =\\sqrt[3]{0.512} \\\\ {x}_{0.512}^{\\frac{1}{2}} & =0.8 \\\\ {x}_{0.512} & =(0.8)^{2} \\\\ {x}_{0.512} & =0.64.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482520 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162000 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "84b181c4-fc23-5a68-8042-55f02b1e5e8a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Percentile of a Continuous Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e85e52c-8e08-56c8-8b37-5f17ff7f2785" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481808} {:answer/id #uuid "13548f7f-10aa-5faa-8652-5d6f71f80b0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481827} {:answer/id #uuid "84c31569-5f15-5e6c-9553-68211785d8f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482083} {:answer/id #uuid "c2733038-517d-5d08-9a0f-39b2b10dae78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482238} {:answer/id #uuid "c753b103-766c-5196-b73c-9776711e2c3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482247}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84c31569-5f15-5e6c-9553-68211785d8f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482083} :answer-field/id #uuid "b10b6ffb-517f-5a7d-bbbf-4ef4514dfdb7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482472}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2f4c7c35-e12b-53f3-8c46-ab140e4e9992" :question/math-academy-id "q-125522" :question/problem "Find the $25$th percentile of the random variable $X$ if the probability distribution function of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2}-1,\\, & 2<x<4, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The $100p$th percentile of a random variable $X$ is the number ${x}_{p}$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X\\le {x}_{p})=p.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we want to find the $25$th percentile, which corresponds to the decimal $p=0.25.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le {x}_{0.25}) & ={\\int }_{2}^{{x}_{0.25}}(\\frac{x}{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-x)|}_{2}^{{x}_{0.25}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}_{0.25}^{2}}{4}-{x}_{0.25}-(\\frac{(2)^{2}}{4}-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}_{0.25}^{2}}{4}-{x}_{0.25}+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $25$th percentile is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}_{0.25}^{2}}{4}-{x}_{0.25}+1 & =0.25 \\\\ {x}_{0.25}^{2}-4{x}_{0.25}+3 & =0 \\\\ ({x}_{0.25}-3)({x}_{0.25}-1) & =0 \\\\ {x}_{0.25}=1,\\,3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we take the root ${x}_{0.25}=3$ because $2<{x}_{0.25}<4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482556 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161999 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "563f7ff5-8ebb-5130-badb-f092fa348959" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quartile of a Continuous Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "211a57e2-d8aa-54b1-beea-511b212443ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.366" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481864} {:answer/id #uuid "59225a5a-4de1-5b47-a565-1141167812b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.666" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481983} {:answer/id #uuid "63d5bd69-c3d3-5125-9e45-bc46319d3648" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.352" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482004} {:answer/id #uuid "a2ccde35-6145-571f-8819-7dd62e2850da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482160} {:answer/id #uuid "eb32e82a-d0cc-5c35-890f-63bb77ee3f7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.636" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482341}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "211a57e2-d8aa-54b1-beea-511b212443ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.366" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481864} :answer-field/id #uuid "e78defba-5c7e-59d1-ab03-e4daad3cbc4a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482495}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7e41b2e9-6ace-571f-a3ef-6f43b41df0ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-125712" :question/problem "Find, to three decimal places, the interquartile range of the random variable $X$ if the cumulative distribution function of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<0, \\\\ {x}^{2},\\, & 0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 1,\\, & x>1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the interquartile range, we first need to find the lower quartile and the upper quartile.\n\nThe lower quartile of a random variable $X$ is the number ${q}_{1}$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X\\le {q}_{1})=\\frac{1}{4},\n$$\n\nand the upper quartile is the number ${q}_{3}$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X\\le {q}_{3})=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the lower quartile:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le {q}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ F({q}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ {q}_{1}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ {q}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we take the root ${q}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}$ because $0\\le {q}_{1}\\le 1.$\n\nThen, we find the upper quartile:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le {q}_{3}) & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ F({q}_{3}) & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ {q}_{3}^{2} & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ {q}_{3} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we take the root ${q}_{3}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ because $0\\le {q}_{3}\\le 1.$\n\nTherefore, the interquartile range is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}IQR & ={q}_{3}-{q}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{2} \\\\  & ≈0.366\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482571 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161999 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "563f7ff5-8ebb-5130-badb-f092fa348959" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quartile of a Continuous Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46b4ec8e-c3e5-5ae6-b5f1-963f8b25be11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.914" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481948} {:answer/id #uuid "498a13e5-8c2e-5df6-a277-b267feb9d7dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.732" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481951} {:answer/id #uuid "eea8253c-9a91-5eee-8af4-be3818d42829" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.646" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482345} {:answer/id #uuid "f0867a0c-eac5-5b6a-a170-f2f1b279db70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.914" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482349} {:answer/id #uuid "fa202739-d377-52d8-acd5-26cb18c3a306" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.914" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482368}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46b4ec8e-c3e5-5ae6-b5f1-963f8b25be11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.914" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481948} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9ae13b6-0cd2-543d-bcb7-22657b86dffb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482477}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a4e71952-c18f-5e5a-8bbb-dfd0f7ad678f" :question/math-academy-id "q-125714" :question/problem "Find, to three decimal places, the interquartile range of the random variable $X$ if the cumulative distribution function of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1, \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}-1}{8}, & 1\\le x\\le 3, \\\\ 1, & x>3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the interquartile range, we first need to find the lower quartile and the upper quartile.\n\nThe lower quartile of a random variable $X$ is the number ${q}_{1}$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X\\le {q}_{1})=\\frac{1}{4},\n$$\n\nand the upper quartile is the number ${q}_{3}$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X\\le {q}_{3})=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the lower quartile:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le {q}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ F({q}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ \\frac{{q}_{1}^{2}-1}{8} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ {q}_{1}^{2}-1 & =2 \\\\ {q}_{1}^{2} & =3 \\\\ {q}_{1} & =\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we take the root ${q}_{1}=\\sqrt{3}$ because $1\\le {q}_{1}\\le 3.$\n\nThen, we find the upper quartile:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le {q}_{3}) & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ F({q}_{3}) & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ \\frac{{q}_{3}^{2}-1}{8} & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ {q}_{3}^{2}-1 & =6 \\\\ {q}_{3}^{2} & =7 \\\\ {q}_{3} & =\\sqrt{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we take the root ${q}_{3}=\\sqrt{7}$ because $1\\le {q}_{3}\\le 3.$\n\nTherefore, the interquartile range is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}IQR & ={q}_{3}-{q}_{1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{3} \\\\  & ≈0.914\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482532 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161999 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "563f7ff5-8ebb-5130-badb-f092fa348959" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quartile of a Continuous Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26b1582a-fe2a-5af4-bba0-1ac6960815b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481874} {:answer/id #uuid "4485f3aa-42b6-5b6c-aa2f-0f673aee9fae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481945} {:answer/id #uuid "955ec2a1-769b-5ec3-89e8-df042128fed6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482126} {:answer/id #uuid "c16c04c9-0dbf-58fd-b26e-3de9324026c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482235} {:answer/id #uuid "c843aa7c-b566-56a4-85c9-ca8a883dcd9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8-\\frac{8\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482252}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c843aa7c-b566-56a4-85c9-ca8a883dcd9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8-\\frac{8\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482252} :answer-field/id #uuid "27de064b-78af-5768-96b1-07df8a910cb1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482400}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3ca6810e-a219-54cd-a8c8-f575cfccdc55" :question/math-academy-id "q-125734" :question/problem "Find the interquartile range of the random variable $X$ if the cumulative distribution function of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<4, \\\\ 1-\\frac{16}{{x}^{2}}, & x\\ge 4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the interquartile range, we first need to find the lower quartile and the upper quartile.\n\nThe lower quartile of a random variable $X$ is the number ${q}_{1}$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X\\le {q}_{1})=\\frac{1}{4},\n$$\n\nand the upper quartile is the number ${q}_{3}$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X\\le {q}_{3})=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the lower quartile:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le {q}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ F({q}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ 1-\\frac{16}{{q}_{1}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ \\frac{16}{{q}_{1}^{2}} & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ {q}_{1} & =\\frac{8\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the upper quartile:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le {q}_{3}) & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ F({q}_{3}) & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ 1-\\frac{16}{{q}_{3}^{2}} & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ \\frac{16}{{q}_{3}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ {q}_{3} & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the interquartile range is\n\n$$\nIQR={q}_{3}-{q}_{1}=8-\\frac{8\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482562 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161998 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a79c4207-c5d6-5386-818e-a7e532492732" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Median Given the PDF a Continuous Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ccc100a-0804-57d3-934a-8576b15919de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481851} {:answer/id #uuid "5056f157-e7ac-5e18-b665-34631b5fa810" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481968} {:answer/id #uuid "6ea8ecb1-b36f-55c1-97dd-23b6b06f366c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14\\sqrt{7}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482030} {:answer/id #uuid "8d19a9c9-2f00-503d-a0ac-b3697e0af0c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482105} {:answer/id #uuid "fd4067de-8e2f-50d3-a556-414aacb24659" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482374}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd4067de-8e2f-50d3-a556-414aacb24659" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482374} :answer-field/id #uuid "14f5578f-6447-52d0-b254-195bbd51df0b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482387}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8d19c0b1-13a1-5100-8957-4c982f273723" :question/math-academy-id "q-125773" :question/problem "Find the median of the random variable $X$ if the probability density function of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{98}{{x}^{3}},\\, & x\\ge 7, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The median of a random variable $X$ is the number $m$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X\\le m)=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le m) & ={\\int }_{7}^{m}\\frac{98}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={-\\frac{49}{{x}^{2}}|}_{7}^{m} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{49}{{m}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the median is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-\\frac{49}{{m}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{49}{{m}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ m & =7\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we took the positive root because $m>7.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162641 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161999 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "563f7ff5-8ebb-5130-badb-f092fa348959" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quartile of a Continuous Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03758742-4e66-5fc5-b8d2-c064330220a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481775} {:answer/id #uuid "28f8e7b0-163f-5d34-82c2-5019a5d8f120" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481879} {:answer/id #uuid "4dcdd795-b4e2-5697-a229-4d5c328622b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481962} {:answer/id #uuid "8a57ef84-dc66-5261-bb34-5e50fd7f3719" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482098} {:answer/id #uuid "ee44477a-a24b-5936-8441-328751567d0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482342}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4dcdd795-b4e2-5697-a229-4d5c328622b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481962} :answer-field/id #uuid "43bc050a-7f4d-5ec6-bef2-a525c0cde7b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186161138}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1e1b7e9e-2574-5316-a0b8-5178c531c66d" :question/math-academy-id "q-94576" :question/problem "Find the interquartile range of the random variable $X$ if the cumulative distribution function of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<1, \\\\ 1-{e}^{1-x},\\, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the interquartile range, we first need to find the lower quartile and the upper quartile.\n\nThe lower quartile of a random variable $X$ is the number ${q}_{1}$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X\\le {q}_{1})=\\frac{1}{4},\n$$\n\nand the upper quartile is the number ${q}_{3}$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X\\le {q}_{3})=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the lower quartile:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le {q}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ F({q}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ 1-{e}^{1-{q}_{1}} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ {e}^{1-{q}_{1}} & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ 1-{q}_{1} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{4}) \\\\ {q}_{1} & =1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{4})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the upper quartile:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le {q}_{3}) & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ F({q}_{3}) & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ 1-{e}^{1-{q}_{3}} & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ {e}^{1-{q}_{3}} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ 1-{q}_{3} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\ {q}_{3} & =1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{4})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the interquartile range is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}IQR & ={q}_{3}-{q}_{1} \\\\  & =1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{4})-(1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{4})) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{4})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482591 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161997 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "84c1cf7c-e334-5173-8ae4-86af0dce56ab" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Median Given the CDF a Continuous Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5012aee4-8029-59e9-a001-1983600f8879" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481966} {:answer/id #uuid "64c196ad-4c8a-588e-b2ff-6bdd2ba18aae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482008} {:answer/id #uuid "6f9dbcca-797e-55ba-8abc-78fc021a5214" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482033} {:answer/id #uuid "bb7b0abc-c581-56fb-bb65-2a52485c0bd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482221} {:answer/id #uuid "bc448948-1a97-5631-ba43-c323b32dee1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482224}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6f9dbcca-797e-55ba-8abc-78fc021a5214" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482033} :answer-field/id #uuid "4273a9c4-b2af-5b72-ac14-00e304bf07b7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482415}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cc24bfb9-272f-54fa-b546-5cdc700f6030" :question/math-academy-id "q-94598" :question/problem "Find the median of the random variable $X$ if the cumulative distribution function of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0, \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}, & 0\\le x\\le 5, \\\\ 1, & x>5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The median of a random variable $X$ is the number $m$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X\\le m)=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nP(X\\le m)=F(m)=\\frac{{m}^{2}}{25},\\,0\\le m\\le 5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the median is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{m}^{2}}{25}=\\frac{1}{2}\\,⇒\\,m=\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{2}}=\\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nNote that we took the positive root because $0\\le m\\le 5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482570 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161997 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "84c1cf7c-e334-5173-8ae4-86af0dce56ab" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Median Given the CDF a Continuous Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "346a0350-155f-58bb-8439-0fb1c2e166bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481903} {:answer/id #uuid "3eb2dba4-a755-55b2-ae4f-bd6ef2d55129" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481930} {:answer/id #uuid "433bcb79-f2e0-5f59-8bbf-c8a6fe6679ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481939} {:answer/id #uuid "5174e0ad-df19-5c17-a6e0-b9f1789a64e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481971} {:answer/id #uuid "7fc44424-4113-54de-a1c7-c3453bbbd004" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482068}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3eb2dba4-a755-55b2-ae4f-bd6ef2d55129" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481930} :answer-field/id #uuid "04eacb23-5651-500e-987d-0658add645b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482380}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a12ce635-7077-5ae6-9899-fd940aea64f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-94601" :question/problem "Find the median of the random variable $X$ if the cumulative distribution function of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0, \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{144}, & 0\\le x\\le 12, \\\\ 1, & x>12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The median of a random variable $X$ is the number $m$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X\\le m)=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nP(X\\le m)=F(m)=\\frac{{m}^{2}}{144},\\,0\\le m\\le 12.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the median is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{m}^{2}}{144}=\\frac{1}{2}\\,⇒\\,m=6\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nNote that we took the positive root because $0\\le m\\le 12.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482548 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161998 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a79c4207-c5d6-5386-818e-a7e532492732" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Median Given the PDF a Continuous Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12b5e394-80fe-57dd-9cb9-ba6e9edd273b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481825} {:answer/id #uuid "1befb3a2-1a61-55a8-b311-dd29e1df21d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481848} {:answer/id #uuid "2c6f4537-9695-5450-99bf-8967143319f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481887} {:answer/id #uuid "36753d1f-fd75-589a-8fb3-f329088220f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481910} {:answer/id #uuid "bd99344b-9ee9-5c83-8690-084c2fcd7f3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482227}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12b5e394-80fe-57dd-9cb9-ba6e9edd273b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481825} :answer-field/id #uuid "188532e0-67bb-558a-be7e-da0adb86d8b6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482390}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "714df0ea-5d53-53df-b0aa-14ba037b9bde" :question/math-academy-id "q-94628" :question/problem "Find the median of the random variable $X$ if the probability density function of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<1, \\\\ \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}},\\, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The median of a random variable $X$ is the number $m$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X\\le m)=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le m) & ={\\int }_{1}^{m}\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{m}\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-3/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{x}^{-1/2}{|}_{1}^{m} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{m}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the median is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{m}} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{m}} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{m} & =2 \\\\ m & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482613 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161998 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a79c4207-c5d6-5386-818e-a7e532492732" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Median Given the PDF a Continuous Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d021253-7df2-5464-9178-35a626b44f93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481890} {:answer/id #uuid "4dc863c8-ca1c-5f30-ab79-a7a81a707dd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{4}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481961} {:answer/id #uuid "73a723a3-8cff-5a15-b741-6f6044bdef48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482043} {:answer/id #uuid "9cba564e-a6ed-532c-983c-2eea1eb2a4db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt[3]{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482147} {:answer/id #uuid "c4d53989-5718-5924-bfd9-3c8e58a253e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482241}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73a723a3-8cff-5a15-b741-6f6044bdef48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482043} :answer-field/id #uuid "e29f424f-71fa-5ce6-a697-ab8b93c418a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482494}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f4cab15e-7525-590b-aa74-c49be38d3cec" :question/math-academy-id "q-94639" :question/problem "Find the median of the random variable $X$ if the probability density function of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<\\frac{1}{2}, \\\\ \\frac{3}{8{x}^{4}},\\, & x\\ge \\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The median of a random variable $X$ is the number $m$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X\\le m)=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le m) & ={\\int }_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{m}\\frac{3}{8{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8{x}^{3}}{|}_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{m} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{8{m}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the median is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-\\frac{1}{8{m}^{3}} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{8{m}^{3}} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {m}^{3} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ m & =\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482517 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161998 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a79c4207-c5d6-5386-818e-a7e532492732" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Median Given the PDF a Continuous Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c4d79bc-915f-5faf-978f-4d42e48a1002" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481886} {:answer/id #uuid "55c24ac5-9fd4-503b-ba36-10fa741c0864" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡6}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481978} {:answer/id #uuid "78eefeb0-a4ae-5e62-bcd9-4a983105c3d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482054} {:answer/id #uuid "793af677-077b-5623-8d55-c294d9651a32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482055} {:answer/id #uuid "e345bb2f-b85f-50d4-b376-0cd925292cbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482313}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "793af677-077b-5623-8d55-c294d9651a32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482055} :answer-field/id #uuid "9860bd94-686f-562b-93e2-7506456e5e9b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482458}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2b515338-9a49-5088-8d83-3ec16988abce" :question/math-academy-id "q-94641" :question/problem "Find the median of the random variable $Y$ if the probability density function of $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}6{e}^{-6y},\\, & y\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The median of a random variable $Y$ is the number $m$ such that\n\n$$\nP(Y\\le m)=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y\\le m) & ={\\int }_{0}^{m}6{e}^{-6y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-{e}^{-6y}{|}_{0}^{m} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-6m}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the median is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-{e}^{-6m} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {e}^{-6m} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -6m & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\ -6m & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ m & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482575 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161998 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a79c4207-c5d6-5386-818e-a7e532492732" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Median Given the PDF a Continuous Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24d9537c-4c6a-5bea-9084-7453673af462" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt[6]{2}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481870} {:answer/id #uuid "363228b0-4656-5329-a192-45892c7d79d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt[6]{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481908} {:answer/id #uuid "5aeaf22f-9630-5a12-b24d-c6bcd8eefbd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt[6]{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481986} {:answer/id #uuid "96e7c5e2-f3f8-5e51-b430-7a56684e572f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[6]{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482130} {:answer/id #uuid "9e404460-a0c2-5106-8aa8-4891726e0ffc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482152}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "363228b0-4656-5329-a192-45892c7d79d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt[6]{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481908} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8a4324b-f75b-536e-a236-773728d8dd8c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482476}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a6d47759-e842-511b-a810-c9880823e33f" :question/math-academy-id "q-94643" :question/problem "Find the median of the random variable $X$ if the probability density function of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<1, \\\\ \\frac{6}{{x}^{7}},\\, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The median of a random variable $X$ is the number $m$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X\\le m)=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le m) & ={\\int }_{1}^{m}\\frac{6}{{x}^{7}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={-\\frac{1}{{x}^{6}}|}_{1}^{m} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{{m}^{6}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the median is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-\\frac{1}{{m}^{6}} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{m}^{6}} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ m & =\\sqrt[6]{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we took the positive root because $m\\ge 1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482602 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161999 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "563f7ff5-8ebb-5130-badb-f092fa348959" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quartile of a Continuous Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "039f35c0-9f74-51e8-b87c-18c9a10f1560" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.855" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481777} {:answer/id #uuid "6b64a068-c831-5808-ab82-de97a974bd21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.845" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482020} {:answer/id #uuid "9b54931e-4f66-558e-ac52-6088a647f3b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.485" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482142} {:answer/id #uuid "b12e960b-3cf9-57eb-a9a7-8546ad220ea8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.885" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482192} {:answer/id #uuid "e6e51d8b-3554-5198-9a2b-299876c96962" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.854" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482326}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b64a068-c831-5808-ab82-de97a974bd21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.845" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482020} :answer-field/id #uuid "21dc5a83-34c9-5825-801d-d29b40f9fa03" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482397}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dfe1ae13-0566-5996-84a0-b50d07468365" :question/math-academy-id "q-94665" :question/problem "Find, to three decimal places, the interquartile range of the random variable $X$ if the cumulative distribution function of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1, \\\\ 1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the interquartile range, we first need to find the lower quartile and the upper quartile.\n\nThe lower quartile of a random variable $X$ is the number ${q}_{1}$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X\\le {q}_{1})=\\frac{1}{4},\n$$\n\nand the upper quartile is the number ${q}_{3}$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X\\le {q}_{3})=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the lower quartile:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le {q}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ F({q}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ 1-\\frac{1}{{{q}_{1}}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{{q}_{1}}^{2}} & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ {q}_{1} & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the upper quartile:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le {q}_{3}) & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ F({q}_{3}) & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ 1-\\frac{1}{{{q}_{3}}^{2}} & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{{q}_{3}}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ {q}_{3} & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the interquartile range is\n\n$$\nIQR={q}_{3}-{q}_{1}=2-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}≈0.845\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482543 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162000 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "84b181c4-fc23-5a68-8042-55f02b1e5e8a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Percentile of a Continuous Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bd0b664-7cd0-5225-8077-d578f99f8c04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481926} {:answer/id #uuid "5b668401-eb08-5c42-9289-5f7254bda777" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481989} {:answer/id #uuid "857e38d3-3ddd-52a6-8559-6963c78e3a81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482086} {:answer/id #uuid "93c6c840-9631-578b-8363-f6b9352ca751" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482122} {:answer/id #uuid "ab4badf2-b2ff-5742-aa22-d9ace53e7565" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482174}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab4badf2-b2ff-5742-aa22-d9ace53e7565" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482174} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2022eed-c29f-583a-a37e-b2d67f6aca04" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482487}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "537b608f-d718-5a66-8b0b-7dabfac0375b" :question/math-academy-id "q-94670" :question/problem "Find the $21$st percentile of the random variable $X$ if the probability distribution function of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{21}x,\\, & 2\\le x\\le 5, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The $100p$th percentile of a random variable $X$ is the number ${x}_{p}$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X\\le {x}_{p})=p.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we want to find the $21$st percentile, which corresponds to the decimal $p=0.21.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le {x}_{0.21}) & ={\\int }_{2}^{{x}_{0.21}}\\frac{2}{21}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{2}}{21}|}_{2}^{{x}_{0.21}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}_{0.21}^{2}}{21}-\\frac{4}{21}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $21$st percentile is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}_{0.21}^{2}}{21}-\\frac{4}{21} & =0.21 \\\\ {x}_{0.21}^{2} & =(0.21)(21)+4 \\\\ {x}_{0.21} & =2.9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162644 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162000 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "84b181c4-fc23-5a68-8042-55f02b1e5e8a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Percentile of a Continuous Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29a3ec05-1796-5998-8e30-938d46d50a1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481881} {:answer/id #uuid "39494504-cec8-5020-9908-1c5cb6914a17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481917} {:answer/id #uuid "3dd3667f-22b1-5593-a711-58ec7a41392e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481929} {:answer/id #uuid "a0567618-3fff-5bf8-8a81-37e04f3d33bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482155} {:answer/id #uuid "fc18e48a-eca0-55b3-8692-d7cfbe38ebd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482372}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc18e48a-eca0-55b3-8692-d7cfbe38ebd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482372} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ef4dfd0-f0cc-51fe-86d6-3a8aa37b7302" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186161156}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7bfa7b9d-151d-5ab9-bbf5-f49790dd348d" :question/math-academy-id "q-94701" :question/problem "Find the $30$th percentile of the random variable $Y$ if the probability distribution function of $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-y},\\, & y\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The $100p$th percentile of a random variable $Y$ is the number ${y}_{p}$ such that\n\n$$\nP(Y\\le {y}_{p})=p.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we want to find the $30$th percentile, which corresponds to the decimal $p=0.3.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y\\le {y}_{0.3}) & ={\\int }_{0}^{{y}_{0.3}}{e}^{-y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-{e}^{-y}{|}_{0}^{{y}_{0.3}} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-{y}_{0.3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $30$th percentile is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-{e}^{-{y}_{0.3}} & =0.3 \\\\ {e}^{-{y}_{0.3}} & =0.7 \\\\ {e}^{-{y}_{0.3}} & =\\frac{7}{10} \\\\ -{y}_{0.3} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{7}{10}) \\\\ {y}_{0.3} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{10}{7}) \\\\ {y}_{0.3} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482505 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162000 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "84b181c4-fc23-5a68-8042-55f02b1e5e8a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Percentile of a Continuous Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44247718-8f4f-58e6-895b-9f3dc89798eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481943} {:answer/id #uuid "89772cdb-fd83-51ae-aa1e-fed0f838a7b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482093} {:answer/id #uuid "b36d7f94-7250-5b44-b690-333886d417f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482196} {:answer/id #uuid "db1bad53-8bf1-579a-bb9d-17ae6d5f1113" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482295} {:answer/id #uuid "dba1842e-1014-5223-9a45-ba19604b7a85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482296}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db1bad53-8bf1-579a-bb9d-17ae6d5f1113" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482295} :answer-field/id #uuid "01c59423-879c-5dcd-b08a-e948d0a753d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482378}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "049efa61-2f95-573c-8d4c-3a15cf157276" :question/math-academy-id "q-94705" :question/problem "Find the $90$th percentile of the random variable $X$ if the probability distribution function of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}},\\, & x\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The $100p$th percentile of a random variable $X$ is the number ${x}_{p}$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X\\le {x}_{p})=p.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we want to find the $90$th percentile, which corresponds to the decimal $p=0.9.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le {x}_{0.9}) & ={\\int }_{1}^{{x}_{0.9}}\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{{x}_{0.9}}\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-3/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{x}^{-1/2}{|}_{1}^{{x}_{0.9}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}_{0.9}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $90$th percentile is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}_{0.9}}} & =0.9 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}_{0.9}}} & =0.1 \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}_{0.9}} & =10 \\\\ {x}_{0.9} & =100.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
